    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="22.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 22.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="302" ed="#liebermann"/>And on þam godcundan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.15"/> gebede syn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.star2"/> VII gebedu; mid þam se ðe hit inweardlice gesingð, he geærndað<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.16"/> to Gode sylfum ymbe æfre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.star2"/> ælce neode, þe man beþearf aðor oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.17"/> for þysu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.18"/></hi> life oððe for ðam toweardan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.19"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="302" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ on þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.8"/> godcundam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.6"/> gebede syn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.9-2"/> seofen gebedu; mid ðam se ðe hit inweardlice gesingð, he geærndað to Gode sylfum ymbe æfre ælce neode, ðe man beðearf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.10"/> aðor oððe for ðissu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> life oððe for ðam toweardan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="302" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ on þam goddcundan gebede synd seofan gebeda; mid þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> se þe hit inweardlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.3"/> gesingþ, geærndað to Gode sylfum ymbe æfre ælce neode, þe man beþearf aðor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.4"/> for ðissum lyfe oððe for þam toweardum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>In qua VII petitiones sunt; et quisquis eam intimo corde cantabit, cum ipso Deo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.9"/> agit de quacumque necessitate uitę presentis et futurę.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>[22, 3] Per ‘Pater noster’ enim potest quisque promereri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.7"/> omne quod necessarium est in hoc sæculo et in futuro.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>In qua Dominica oracione continentur VII preces; quibus qui attento animo orauerit, seruiet legacionem ad Deum, pro qualibet necessitate facit, tam presentis uite quam future.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="22.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="170" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ on þam godcunda[n]<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#ICn_22-3.robnote.fn.10"/> gebede syn<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#ICn_22-3.robnote.fn.11"/> seofen gebedu mid ðam se ðe hit inweardlice gesingð he geærndað to Gode sylfum ymbe æfre ælce neode ðe man beðearf aðor oððe for ðissum life oððe for ðam toweardan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="250" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And on þam godcundan gebede syn VII gebedu; mid þam se ðe hit inweardlice gesingð, he geærndað to Gode sylfum ymbe æfre ælce neode, þe man beþearf aðor oððe for þysum life oððe for ðam toweardan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="303" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.de.1"/> in diesem göttlichen Gebete sind sieben Bitten; durch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.de.2"/> sie wendet sich, wer es innig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.de.3"/> hersagt, an Gott selbst um jegliche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_22-3.lnote.de.4"/> Nothdurft, die man bedarf entweder für dieses oder für das zukünftige Leben.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And in that divine prayer there are seven petitions; with them, whoever sings it inwardly intercedes with God himself for every need that one has, either for this life or for the life to come.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="171" ed="#robertson"/>And in that sacred prayer there are seven petitions<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_22-3.robnote.n.1"/>, and he who recites it from the depths of his heart inwardly makes supplication thereby to God himself for everything of which a man has need, both for this life and for the life to come.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="251" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And in that holy prayer are seven entreaties; he who recites it in his soul pleads with God himself concerning all things which may be to a person’s benefit, both in this life and in the life to come.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="303">Wulfstan p. 20; Wulfstan p. 21</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. | ebd. 21</note>
        <note type="editorial">In A the text begins S. 46 with the red heading ‘Cnutes lage’. Liebermann compares Wulfstan p. 21.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 303, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dam g. synd seofan gebeoda <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dam g. synd seofan gebeoda Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Napier</hi> Über Wulfstan 62. 66</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Napier Über Wulfstan 62. 66</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rend. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rend. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þissum lyfe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þissum lyfe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rdum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rdum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">303</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Deus <hi rend="italic">K; fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Deus K; lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">303</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> feret?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read feret?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">beginnt S.</hi> 46, <hi rend="italic">roth überschr.</hi> Cnutes lage</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. 46 begins, with the heading Cnutes lage in red</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. in</hi> synd</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered in the 16th cent. to synd</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> ðeð.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from ðeð.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">303</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mereri <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mereri Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d <hi rend="italic">übergeschrieben</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">302</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ador <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ador A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Vater unser 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Vater unser 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘indem’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘in that’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘bei sich, im Ggs. zu laut’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘inwardly, as opposed to aloud’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_22-3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">201</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Eine Hs. Wulfstans ändert Wortstellung in <hi rend="italic">æfre ymbe</hi>; aber <hi rend="italic">æfre ælc</hi> ist der Vorgänger des heutigen <hi rend="italic">every</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">One MS of Wulfstan changes the word order to <hi rend="italic">æfre ymbe</hi>; but <hi rend="italic">æfre ælc</hi> is the forerunner of modern <hi rend="italic">every</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_22-3.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Ancren Riwle</hi>, ed. Morton, London, 1853, p. 28.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_22-3.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">170</biblScope></bibl><label>godcunda[n</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">G, A; <hi rend="italic">-am</hi> B, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_22-3.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">170</biblScope></bibl><label>syn</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Changed later to <hi rend="italic">synd.</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
